        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Remove incorrect claim that URL inputs support 'multiple' attribute]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42023</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42023"/>
        <updated>2025-11-19T21:07:40.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9015024?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Corrected the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Guides/Constraint_validation#semantic_input_types" rel="nofollow">Semantic input types</a>  section to clarify that the multiple attribute applies to email inputs but not url inputs.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">The documentation previously stated both email and url inputs support the multiple attribute for comma-separated lists.  However, according to the HTML Standard, the multiple attribute is not supported for <code class="notranslate">&lt;input type="url"&gt;</code>. This update aligns the guide with the specification.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #42005.">Fixes</span>  <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3639467668" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42005" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/42005/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42005">#42005</a></p>



]]></content>
