    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Enhance documentation for 'object-fit' CSS property]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42014</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42014"/>
        <updated>2025-11-19T12:20:24.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177507094?u=02fca01b2bde41566660e171c995c01443421086&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">Include a note on the importance of setting <code class="notranslate">width</code> and <code class="notranslate">height</code> for effective <code class="notranslate">object-fit</code> application.</p>


<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>

<p dir="auto">I added a note about how to use the <code class="notranslate">object-fit</code> property effectively</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>

<ul dir="auto">
<li>Because I lost a lot of time trying to understand why the <code class="notranslate">object-fit</code> property doesn't work on my personal examples, I did what the docs instruct, but that property fails to apply. And just later I discovered that I should set a <strong>height</strong> and <strong>width</strong> to the image in order for that <code class="notranslate">object-fit</code> to be applied effectively. I think that works the same for all the replaced-elements, but I only tested it for <code class="notranslate">img</code> elements.</li>
<li>Readers will be able to use that <code class="notranslate">object-fit</code> effectively.</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>

<p dir="auto">There is no clue or note about that even in the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/object-fit" rel="nofollow">object-fit mdn-reference</a></p>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>



]]></content>
